  {\n            \"summary\": \"Quinolones impact liver function and cardiac electrophysiology\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond systemic reactions, quinolone antibiotics demonstrate specific organ toxicities. Hepatic effects include transient elevations in liver function biochemical indicators, typically resolving after discontinuation [Data: Relationships (1437)]. Cardiac toxicity, particularly QT interval prolongation, is a well-documented risk—especially with fourth-generation quinolones—and poses a serious threat in susceptible individuals [Data: Relationships (5997, 6003)]. This arrhythmogenic potential mandates ECG monitoring in high-risk patients and avoidance of concomitant use with other QT-prolonging agents like amiodarone or tricyclic antidepressants. These targeted organ toxicities reinforce the need for baseline and periodic laboratory and electrocardiographic assessments during treatment.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the widespread clinical use of quinolones combined with their potential to cause serious, multi-system adverse reactions in vulnerable populations.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782127341, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1414, "prompt_tokens": 7012, "total_tokens": 8426, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Quinolone Drug Class and Associated Adverse Reactions\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on the drug class '喹诺酮类药物' (Quinolone antibiotics), which is indicated for treating infectious diseases but is 